{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/letian_fu/status/2096673034325381268","id":"2096673034325381268","text":"1. It is exciting to benchmark the capability of multimodal models to perform continuous control on robots, but harnesses + tool calls (IK, SAM3, etc.) can achieve the same result far cheaper, faster, and more reliable.   \n\n2. Self-evolving harnesses and skill libraries will rapidly expand the Pareto frontier of what these models are capable of. VLA and WAM will be part of these libraries.   \n\n3. Robotics (and in general, applications in the physical world) is the next frontier of multimodal models and agents 🚀🚀  \n\nI was very fortunate to explore this direction with @Ken_Goldberg @DrJimFan @yukez @trevordarrell at Berkeley and Nvidia with many of my friends over the past year. Can’t wait to see how this field evolves!","raw_text":{"text":"1. It is exciting to benchmark the capability of multimodal models to perform continuous control on robots, but harnesses + tool calls (IK, SAM3, etc.) can achieve the same result far cheaper, faster, and more reliable.   \n\n2. Self-evolving harnesses and skill libraries will rapidly expand the Pareto frontier of what these models are capable of. VLA and WAM will be part of these libraries.   \n\n3. Robotics (and in general, applications in the physical world) is the next frontier of multimodal models and agents 🚀🚀  \n\nI was very fortunate to explore this direction with @Ken_Goldberg @DrJimFan @yukez @trevordarrell at Berkeley and Nvidia with many of my friends over the past year. Can’t wait to see how this field evolves!","display_text_range":[0,729],"facets":[{"type":"mention","indices":[573,586],"original":"Ken_Goldberg","id":"89583009"},{"type":"mention","indices":[587,596],"original":"DrJimFan","id":"1007413134"},{"type":"mention","indices":[597,603],"original":"yukez","id":"15751831"},{"type":"mention","indices":[604,618],"original":"trevordarrell","id":"16119933"}]},"author":{"screen_name"